ding</h3>
    <div data-type="exercise" id="fs-id1167067296819" class="os-exercise"><header></header><section>
      <div data-type="problem" id="fs-id1167067296749">
<span class="os-number">13</span><span class="os-divider">. </span>
<div class="os-problem-container">
<p id="fs-id1164565515272">True or false—The efficiency of a simple machine is always less than 100 percent because some small fraction of the input work is always converted to heat energy due to friction.</p>
<ol id="fs-id1164566347808" type="a">
<li>True</li>
<li>False</li></ol>
<!--        <para id="fs-id1167067043779">
          <link class="os-embed" url="#ost/api/ex/k12phys-ch09-ex045"/>
        </para>-->
      </div>
</div>
    </section></div>
    <div data-type="exercise" id="fs-id1167066847645" class="os-exercise"><header></header><section>
      <div data-type="problem" id="fs-id1167067267984">
<span class="os-number">14</span><span class="os-divider">. </span>
<div class="os-problem-container">
<p id="fs-id1164567494063">The circular handle of a faucet is attached to a rod that opens and closes a valve when the handle is turned. If the rod has a diameter of 1 cm and the IMA of the machine is 6, what is the radius of the handle?</p>
<ol id="fs-id1164567846480" type="A">
<li>0.08 cm</li>
<li>0.17 cm</li>
<li>3.0 cm</li>
<li>6.0 cm</li></ol>

<!--        <para id="fs-id1167067039075">
          <link class="os-embed" url="#ost/api/ex/k12phys-ch09-ex046"/>
        </para>-->
      </div>
</div>
    </section></div>
